# Frontend & UI Audit — Gaps & Recommendations

## Current State

The `@aevryn/ui` package is a **premium component library** (9/10). The `apps/web` workspace that uses it is a **hardcoded prototype** (3/10).

---

## 1. Workspace Page — What Exists vs What's Needed

### File: `apps/web/src/app/workspace/page.tsx` (323 lines)

**Current:** Static hardcoded demo messages. No backend integration.

```tsx
// Line 109-115 — hardcoded user message
<ChatMessage from="user" time="Wednesday 6:06 PM" actions={actions}>
  Hi who are you an what can you do
</ChatMessage>
```

**Needed:** Dynamic message list from `getThread` tRPC query.

### Required Changes

#### 1a. Thread State Management (Zustand)

Create stores:

```ts
// stores/thread-store.ts
interface ThreadStore {
  threads: ThreadListItem[];
  activeThreadId: string | null;
  setActiveThread: (id: string) => void;
  createThread: () => void;
}

// stores/message-store.ts
interface MessageStore {
  messages: ChatMessage[];
  addMessage: (msg: ChatMessage) => void;
  updateMessage: (id: string, patch: Partial<ChatMessage>) => void;
}

// stores/workflow-store.ts
interface WorkflowStore {
  workflowId: string | null;
  status: ExecutionStatus | null;
  activity: ActivitySnapshot | null;
  plan: Plan | null;
  planProgress: PlanProgress | null;
  approvals: Approval[];
}

// stores/ui-store.ts
interface UIStore {
  isStreaming: boolean;
  thinkingIndicator: boolean;
  showSidebar: boolean;
}
```

#### 1b. Wire ChatComposer to tRPC

**Current:** `ChatComposer` calls a fake `respond()` function (line 87-100 of chat-composer.tsx).

**Needed:**

```tsx
const sendMessage = trpc.agent.sendMessage.useMutation();
const handleSend = (text: string, files: File[]) => {
  sendMessage.mutate({ message: text, workflowId });
  addMessage({ id: crypto.randomUUID(), from: "user", text, files });
};
```

#### 1c. Uncomment QueryClientProvider

**File:** `apps/web/src/components/providers.tsx` (line 18-21)

```tsx
// Currently commented out:
{
  /* <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}> */
}
{
  children;
}
{
  /* </QueryClientProvider> */
}
```

**Fix:** Uncomment. Required for tRPC queries to work.

#### 1d. Thread URL Routing

**Current:** `/workspace` shows the demo page. `/workspace/[threadId]` is a stub.

**Needed:**

- `/workspace` → shows thread list or "create new thread" state
- `/workspace/[threadId]` → loads thread via `getThread` query, renders chat
- On first message in new thread: create workflow, redirect to `/workspace/[workflowId]`

```tsx
// apps/web/src/app/workspace/[threadId]/page.tsx
export default function ThreadPage({
  params,
}: {
  params: { threadId: string };
}) {
  const { data: thread } = trpc.agent.getThread.useQuery({
    workflowId: params.threadId,
  });
  // Render chat from thread.turns
}
```

---

## 2. Component Usage Gaps

### 2a. ThinkingSteps — Not Wired to Real Data

**File:** `apps/web/src/components/workspace/tool-step-calls.tsx`

Four hardcoded components: `ResearchAgent`, `WebScrapeAgent`, `CompilingAgent`, `FinalAnswerStep`. These use `ThinkingSteps` with static data.

**Needed:** Dynamic step rendering from `activity.tools[]` and `activity.steps[]`:

```tsx
function ActivitySteps({ activity }: { activity: ActivitySnapshot }) {
  return (
    <ThinkingSteps>
      <ThinkingStepsHeader>
        {activity.currentActivity ?? "Running..."}
      </ThinkingStepsHeader>
      <ThinkingStepsContent>
        {activity.tools.map((tool) => (
          <ThinkingStep
            key={tool.order}
            icon={toolIcon(tool.tool)}
            label={toolLabel(tool.tool)}
            status={
              tool.status === "completed"
                ? "complete"
                : tool.status === "running"
                  ? "active"
                  : "pending"
            }
          />
        ))}
      </ThinkingStepsContent>
    </ThinkingSteps>
  );
}
```

### 2b. ThinkingIndicator — Not Triggered

**File:** `packages/ui/src/components/ui/thinking-indicator.tsx`

Exists in the demo (line 254-256 of workspace page) but never triggered by real backend state.

**Needed:** Show when `workflowStore.status === "running"` and no messages have been received yet for the current turn.

### 2c. SystemMessage — Not Used Dynamically

**File:** `packages/ui/src/components/ui/system-message.tsx`

Used in demo for hardcoded error/warning. Should render:

- Recovery attempts (from `thread.recoveryAttempts`)
- Execution failures (from `execution.status === "failed"`)
- Approval requests (from `thread.approvals`)

### 2d. QuestionFlow — Not Wired

**File:** `packages/ui/src/components/question-flow.tsx`

Used in demo (line 164) but not connected to LLM's question-asking flow.

**Needed:** When the agent returns a `question` decision (future), render `QuestionFlow` with the questions. Currently the agent doesn't emit questions — it plans via the planning mode.

### 2e. AccordionGroup — Plan Review

**File:** Demo uses it for plan review (line 188-204). Needs to render `thread.plan.steps[]`:

```tsx
{
  thread.plan?.steps?.map((step, i) => (
    <AccordionItem key={i} value={`step-${i}`} index={i}>
      <AccordionTrigger>
        Step {i + 1}: {step}
      </AccordionTrigger>
      <AccordionContent>
        {thread.planProgress?.currentStep === i
          ? "In progress"
          : thread.planProgress?.currentStep > i
            ? "Completed"
            : "Pending"}
      </AccordionContent>
    </AccordionItem>
  ));
}
```

### 2f. Table — LLM Output

**File:** Demo shows a hardcoded table. LLMs return markdown tables, not HTML.

**Needed:** Markdown parser (react-markdown + remark-gfm) to render tables, code blocks, lists from LLM output.

---

## 3. Missing UI Components

### 3a. Run / Stop / Pause Buttons

**Current:** Header has `Run` and `More` buttons (line 89-91) — both non-functional.

**Needed:**

```tsx
// Run button: calls confirmWorkflow (if draft) or runWorkflow (if active)
<Button onClick={() => {
  if (workflow.status === "draft") confirmWorkflow.mutate({ workflowId });
  else runWorkflow.mutate({ workflowId });
}}>Run</Button>

// Stop button: shows when status is "running"
<Button variant="destructive" onClick={() => stopWorkflow.mutate({ workflowId })}>
  Stop
</Button>

// Pause button: shows when status is "running"
<Button onClick={() => pauseWorkflow.mutate({ workflowId })}>Pause</Button>
```

### 3b. "More" Dialog

**Current:** `More` button exists (line 91) with a comment about sharing and prompts.

**Needed:** A dialog (similar to `SettingsDialog`) with:

- **Sharing tab:** Share thread link, export thread
- **Prompts tab:** System prompt, additional instructions, question history
- **Memory tab:** View/manage per-thread memory entries

Pattern already exists in `SettingsDialog` (dialog + sidebar + scroll area).

### 3c. Notification Bell

**Current:** No notification UI anywhere.

**Needed:** Bell icon in header with unread count badge. Click opens notification list.

Backend already has: `unreadNotifications` query, `listNotifications` query, `markNotificationsRead` mutation.

### 3d. Approval Flow UI

**Current:** No approval UI.

**Needed:** When `activity.status === "awaiting_approval"`:

- Show approval card with tool name, input preview
- Approve/Deny buttons
- Calls `resolveApproval` mutation

### 3e. Thread List / Sidebar

**Current:** `AppSidebar` uses hardcoded `NAV_SECTIONS` from `nav-data.ts`.

**Needed:** Replace with real data from `listThreads` (new endpoint) or `listRuns`.

```tsx
// In AppSidebar
const { data: threads } = trpc.agent.listRuns.useQuery({ limit: 50 });
// Map to NavSection items with real statuses
```

### 3f. Activity Indicator (Thick Indicator)

**Current:** `ThinkingIndicator` exists but is a morphing SVG. User wants a "thick indicator" — a prominent status bar showing the agent is working.

**Needed:** A status bar below the header or above the composer:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ ● Running searchWeb... (Step 2/5, 3 tools) │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Use `activity.currentActivity`, `activity.steps.length`, `activity.tools.length`.

---

## 4. Chat Message Rendering

### Current Problem

The `getThread` query returns:

- `turns[].execution.prompt` — user message
- `turns[].steps[].text` — assistant message (from `assistantText`)
- `turns[].toolExecutions[]` — tool calls per step

But the frontend has no logic to map this to chat bubbles.

### Proposed Mapping

```
For each turn (chronological):
  1. Render user message: turn.execution.prompt
  2. For each step in turn.steps:
     a. If step has toolCalls → render ThinkingSteps (tool activity)
     b. If step.text → render assistant ChatMessage with step.text
  3. If turn.execution.status is not terminal → render ThinkingIndicator
```

### Message Types in Chat

| Source                     | Render As                                  |
| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| `execution.prompt`         | User ChatMessage                           |
| `step.assistantText`       | Assistant ChatMessage                      |
| `step.toolCalls`           | ThinkingSteps (collapsible tool activity)  |
| `activity.currentActivity` | ThinkingIndicator (when running)           |
| `recoveryAttempts[]`       | SystemMessage (warning, with attempt info) |
| `approvals[]`              | ApprovalCard (pending)                     |
| `plan`                     | AccordionGroup (plan review)               |
| `planProgress`             | ProgressBar (step progress)                |
| `notifications[]`          | SystemMessage (info)                       |

---

## 5. useIcons Hook Adoption

**File:** `packages/ui/src/lib/icon-context.tsx`

The `useIcon` / `useIcons` hooks provide a consistent icon system. Currently used in:

- `app-sidebar.tsx` (15+ icons)
- `chat-composer.tsx` (2 icons)
- `settings-dialog.tsx` (5+ icons)

NOT used in:

- `tool-step-calls.tsx` — uses lucide-react directly
- `workspace/page.tsx` — uses lucide-react directly (CopyIcon, RotateCcwIcon, PlayIcon)

**Fix:** Replace direct lucide-react imports with `useIcon` for consistency:

```tsx
// Before
import { CopyIcon, RotateCcwIcon } from "lucide-react";

// After
const CopyIcon = useIcon("copy");
const RotateIcon = useIcon("rotate-ccw");
```

---

## 6. Component Reuse Opportunities

### 6a. QueuedStack — Already Built

`QueuedStack` in `packages/ui/src/components/queued-stack.tsx` handles message queuing during streaming. Already wired in `ChatComposer`. Just needs real backend integration.

### 6b. DropdownMenu — For "More" Dialog

The `DropdownMenu` component (720 lines) is overkill for the "More" button. Use the `Dialog` + `Sidebar` pattern from `SettingsDialog` instead.

### 6c. Surface/Shape/Size Contexts

Design token contexts (`useSurface`, `useShape`, `useSize`) are available but rarely used outside the sidebar. Components should use them for consistent elevation and spacing.

---

## 7. Missing CSS/Style Integration

### 7a. `shimmer-text` Class

Used in `ThinkingStep` for active steps (thinking-steps.tsx). Ensure it's defined in globals.css.

### 7b. Status Colors

`nav-data.ts` uses `ExecutionStatus` for sidebar items. The status-to-color mapping should be consistent across:

- Sidebar nav items
- Activity indicator
- Plan progress bar
- Notification badges

---

## 8. Priority Order for Frontend Work

| #   | Task                                  | Depends On | Effort  |
| --- | ------------------------------------- | ---------- | ------- |
| 1   | Uncomment QueryClientProvider         | Nothing    | Trivial |
| 2   | Create Zustand stores                 | Nothing    | Medium  |
| 3   | Wire ChatComposer to tRPC sendMessage | #1, #2     | Small   |
| 4   | Implement getThread rendering         | #1, #2     | Medium  |
| 5   | Thread URL routing                    | #3, #4     | Medium  |
| 6   | Real-time polling for activity        | #4         | Medium  |
| 7   | Run/Stop/Pause buttons                | #3         | Small   |
| 8   | Thread list in sidebar                | #1         | Medium  |
| 9   | Plan progress visualization           | #4         | Small   |
| 10  | Notification bell + list              | #1         | Medium  |
| 11  | Approval flow UI                      | #4         | Medium  |
| 12  | "More" dialog                         | Nothing    | Medium  |
| 13  | Markdown parser                       | #4         | Medium  |
| 14  | Activity indicator (thick)            | #6         | Small   |
| 15  | useIcons adoption                     | Nothing    | Small   |

# Schema Proposals — Chat, Threads, Messages, Workflows

## Current State

No dedicated "thread" or "message" tables. A thread IS a workflow. Messages are derived from `execution.prompt` (user) + `step.assistantText` (assistant).

---

## Proposed Chat Message Schema

### Option A: Derive from Existing Tables (Recommended)

No new tables needed. Map from existing data:

```ts
// Derive chat messages from getThread response
interface ChatMessage {
  id: string; // execution.id (user msg) or step.id (assistant msg)
  role: "user" | "assistant";
  content: string; // execution.prompt or step.text
  timestamp: Date; // execution.startedAt or step.createdAt
  metadata?: {
    executionId?: string;
    stepId?: string;
    toolCalls?: ToolCallSummary[];
    cost?: number;
    tokens?: number;
  };
}

// Rendering logic
function deriveMessages(thread: ThreadData): ChatMessage[] {
  const messages: ChatMessage[] = [];
  for (const turn of thread.turns) {
    // User message
    if (turn.prompt) {
      messages.push({
        id: turn.execution.id,
        role: "user",
        content: turn.prompt,
        timestamp: turn.execution.startedAt,
      });
    }
    // Assistant messages (one per step)
    for (const step of turn.steps) {
      if (step.text) {
        messages.push({
          id: step.id,
          role: "assistant",
          content: step.text,
          timestamp: step.createdAt,
          metadata: {
            executionId: turn.execution.id,
            stepId: step.id,
            toolCalls: step.toolCalls?.map((tc) => ({
              name: tc.toolName,
              status: tc.status,
              durationMs: tc.provider?.durationMs,
            })),
          },
        });
      }
    }
  }
  return messages;
}
```

### Option B: Dedicated Message Table (Future)

If you need reactions, edits, pins, or threaded replies:

```sql
CREATE TABLE chat_message (
  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,           -- msg_ prefix
  workflow_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES workflow(id),
  execution_id TEXT REFERENCES workflow_execution(id),
  step_id TEXT REFERENCES workflow_step(id),
  role TEXT NOT NULL,             -- 'user' | 'assistant' | 'system'
  content TEXT NOT NULL,
  metadata JSONB,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
  updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE INDEX idx_chat_message_workflow ON chat_message(workflow_id, created_at);
```

**Recommendation:** Start with Option A. Add Option B only when you need message-level features (reactions, edits, pins).

---

## Thread Schema

A "thread" is already a `workflow` record. The `getThread` query assembles the full picture:

```ts
// getThread response shape (already implemented)
interface ThreadData {
  workflow: {
    id: string; // wf_xxx
    objective: string;
    status: WorkflowStatus;
    createdAt: Date;
  };
  plan: Plan | null; // { title, objective, summary, steps[] }
  planProgress: PlanProgress | null; // { currentStep, status, note }
  activity: ActivitySnapshot | null; // { status, currentActivity, steps[], tools[] }
  turns: TurnData[]; // chronological execution records
  approvals: ApprovalData[];
  schedules: ScheduleData[];
  notifications: NotificationData[];
  observations: ObservationData[];
  recoveryAttempts: RecoveryData[];
  memorySummary: MemoryEntry[] | null;
}
```

### Thread List Schema

```ts
// For sidebar rendering
interface ThreadListItem {
  id: string;
  title: string; // from plan.title or workflow.objective (truncated)
  status: ExecutionStatus; // drives sidebar indicator color
  lastActivity: Date; // most recent execution startedAt or step createdAt
  unreadCount: number; // notifications not read
  stepProgress?: {
    // if plan exists
    completed: number;
    total: number;
  };
}
```

---

## Activity Snapshot Schema (Already Exists)

**File:** `packages/workflow/src/schemas.ts:88-117`

```ts
interface ActivitySnapshot {
  status:
    | "running"
    | "completed"
    | "failed"
    | "sleeping"
    | "waiting"
    | "awaiting_approval"
    | "paused";
  currentActivity?: string; // "running searchWeb", "summarizing"
  executionId?: string;
  steps: Array<{ order: number; text: string }>;
  tools: Array<{
    order: number;
    step: number;
    tool: string;
    status: "running" | "completed" | "failed";
  }>;
  updatedAt: Date;
}
```

### Proposed Enhancements

Add `substeps` for nested tool activity:

```ts
interface ActivitySnapshot {
  // ... existing fields
  totalStepsPlanned?: number; // from plan.steps.length
  currentStepIndex?: number; // from planProgress.currentStep
  estimatedTimeRemaining?: number; // ms, optional
}
```

---

## Plan Progress Schema (Already Exists)

**File:** `packages/workflow/src/schemas.ts:145-151`

```ts
interface PlanProgress {
  currentStep: number; // 0-indexed, steps completed
  status: "in_progress" | "completed";
  note?: string; // optional context
